# Why vendored (not fetched at run time): Orodruin has no Internet egress
# (docs/design/orodruin-contract.md) — every atomic an injector runs must already be inside
# the image that `make orodruin-push` loads. The whole upstream tree is not vendored: it is
# large and mostly Windows; we keep only the techniques the catalog marks `implemented`.
#
# How they are used: annatar/engines/atomic.py reads the test's `command` and
# `cleanup_command` by its `auto_generated_guid`, substitutes the input-argument defaults,
# and runs them in the enrolled target VM through Azure Run Command (every call journaled by
# the Orodruin contract). We do NOT run the upstream invoke-atomicredteam runner — the
# adapter is the only thing that reads these files.
